From 2e7f788568aad628017eee054aaec293bfe0c905 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:57:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(pathkernel): the medial line, trace and helix guide
 planners

Sub-PR 2 of 2 of K2 (#4176) on side/path-kernel:
- MedialPlanner: the medial axis of the cutter-centre area (new
  Region::medial_axis in camcraft-geometry: Voronoi of the sampled
  boundary via a Bowyer-Watson Delaunay, theta-pruned, RDP-simplified).
- TracePlanner on a new KernelRegion::Chains (chain_region): the chains
  at a left/right/zero offset (new geo2d::offset_side for open chains),
  the keep-out stretches left out and named.
- Exact circle rings of a hole (RingsChoice with a circle) and
  HelixPlanner (GuideChoice::Helix, Curve::helix with its Lead).
- Guides plans every family; FAMILY_NOT_YET and CIRCLE_NOT_YET are gone.

Pinned by the laws suite (guide_medial, guide_trace, guide_helix,
guide_laws: L1-L4) and the motion pins kernel_guides against the #4153
goldens. Decisions: docs/decisions/4176-kernel-guides-medial-trace-helix.md.

Refs #4176

